cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Democratize Security: a research harness for functional and secure code from AI coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Democratize Security Authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dillaryclump/democratize-security"
url: "https://github.com/dillaryclump/democratize-security"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0.dev0
abstract: >-
  A research harness that measures whether AI coding agents produce code that is
  both functional and secure. The first property is tenant isolation in a
  FastAPI and PostgreSQL service. It contains a reference application protected
  by row-level security, an independent verifier with deliberately unsafe
  controls, agent tasks graded from sealed artifacts in a separate container, a
  durable ledger with per-request model cost metering, and a pre-registered pilot
  protocol. As of November 2026 the pilot is incomplete and no benefit of the
  security integration has been demonstrated.
keywords:
  - AI coding agents
  - LLM evaluation
  - secure code generation
  - tenant isolation
  - multi-tenancy
  - PostgreSQL row-level security
  - FastAPI
  - access control
